{"visualAudit":"02-candidates","data":{"grades":[{"subjectMatch":2,"learningValue":1,"composition":2,"thumbnailClarity":1,"contextualFit":1,"problems":["Earthworks not visible; sheep and sky dominate","Photographer's own caption admits the earthworks need an aerial view"],"reason":"Verified as the Griff deserted village site, but the pixels show a grassy ridge with sheep. The humps and bumps the Overview describes cannot be seen.","id":"13153233","total":7,"accepted":false},{"subjectMatch":2,"learningValue":1,"composition":2,"thumbnailClarity":1,"contextualFit":1,"problems":["Earthworks not distinguishable at thumbnail size","Aircraft wing intrudes at right","Shows a living farm and village, not a deserted site"],"reason":"The aerial view of Stainton le Vale is dominated by fields and an inhabited farmstead. No clear earthworks show, so it fails to illustrate what remains of a deserted village.","id":"187662087","total":7,"accepted":false},{"subjectMatch":2,"learningValue":1,"composition":1,"thumbnailClarity":1,"contextualFit":1,"problems":["Hazy, distant view","Aircraft wing intrudes at left","Earthworks not visible"],"reason":"A distant, hazy patchwork of fields with no discernible village earthworks. It is weaker than the other aerial views.","id":"187662114","total":6,"accepted":false},{"subjectMatch":2,"learningValue":1,"composition":2,"thumbnailClarity":1,"contextualFit":1,"problems":["Earthworks not clearly visible","Visible stripes look like modern field marks, not house platforms"],"reason":"This is the cleanest aerial frame, but it shows ordinary fields and hedges. No identifiable village earthworks appear, so it cannot show readers the traces the Overview describes. Reject all four candidates.","id":"188026490","total":7,"accepted":false}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5-5","images":[{"id":"13153233","title":"Deserted Medieval Village of Griff - geograph.org.uk - 615670.jpg","description":"Deserted Medieval Village of Griff A field of well preserved humps and bumps give away where the village once stood. It was probably cleared during the construction of the grange farm to the east (now Griff Farm). Unfortunately it really needs an aerial view to show the earthworks to their best so on this occasion the sheep were more photogenic. \nThe site is designated as Open Access land under DEFRA's farm conservation scheme.","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b4/Deserted_Medieval_Village_of_Griff_-_geograph.org.uk_-_615670.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deserted_Medieval_Village_of_Griff_-_geograph.org.uk_-_615670.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Deserted_Medieval_Village_of_Griff_-_geograph.org.uk_-_615670.jpg/500px-Deserted_Medieval_Village_of_Griff_-_geograph.org.uk_-_615670.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","creator":"Mick Garratt","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"},{"id":"187662087","title":"Deserted Medieval Earthworks, Stainton le Vale, aerial 2026 (1) - geograph.org.uk - 8261312.jpg","description":"Deserted Medieval Earthworks, Stainton le Vale: aerial 2026 (1)","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e7/Deserted_Medieval_Earthworks%2C_Stainton_le_Vale%2C_aerial_2026_%281%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_8261312.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deserted_Medieval_Earthworks,_Stainton_le_Vale,_aerial_2026_(1)_-_geograph.org.uk_-_8261312.jpg","displayUrl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Deserted_Medieval_Earthworks%2C_Stainton_le_Vale%2C_aerial_2026_%281%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_8261312.jpg/500px-Deserted_Medieval_Earthworks%2C_Stainton_le_Vale%2C_aerial_2026_%281%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_8261312.jpg?utm_source=common